# Video masters. These live outside public/ so they are never served;
# assets/*.src.* is the convention (see also assets/about-3d-man.src.glb).
# The Netflix master is a 476MB broadcast delivery - too large for GitHub,
# and there is nothing in it the web cut does not have.
assets/netflix-mi.src.mp4
# The Work tab's case study films, moved out of public/ so a deploy never
# ships them: 990MB of broadcast masters that only the build reads.
# The wall takes one frame out of each; nothing serves the file itself.
assets/bhim-upi.src.mp4
assets/dhurandhar-2.src.mp4
assets/made-in-titan.src.mp4
assets/special-ops-2.src.mp4

# The client's delivery folder, whole. It used to sit under public/, which
# meant a deploy shipped 2GB of broadcast masters and print-size exports
# for a site that serves 160MB - and a file under public/ is served whether
# or not anything links to it. Nothing does any more: every picture and
# film the site draws now comes out of a derived folder next to it
# (/assets/ai, /assets/art, /assets/home, /assets/work/*, /assets/sfx),
# written by the scripts in scripts/ and committed. This is what those
# scripts read.
#
# It is not in the repo, so a fresh clone cannot re-run them. That is the
# same arrangement the video masters above are already under, and it is
# the right one: the derived output is committed, so a clone builds and
# deploys fine - it just cannot regenerate an asset until somebody puts
# the delivery folder back beside it.
assets/SC Website Revamp/
